# No dense layer on the factorial's candidate (factorial.bux's r1v1k1f0p0s0: the
# late-2026 hybrid with hyper-connections, the value residual and the key-value conv).
# The candidate's first layer has a dense SwiGLU and every later one the experts, as
# every 2026 model of the study: 2024 DeepSeekMoE and DeepSeek-V2 keep 1 layer dense,
# DeepSeek-V3 3, 2025 Kimi K2 1 and GLM-4.5 3, for the routing and load balance of
# the first layers, which DeepSeekMoE finds converge slowest. A token's 7 experts and
# the shared one are about as wide as the dense SwiGLU, so the arm keeps about the
# active parameters and adds a layer of experts' total ones. More dense layers would
# be most of a model of 8 or 12 layers, so the arm tests none against one. Everything
# else is the candidate's, so it pairs with it by seed.
use m2026_hybrid
use timeline_code
use rungs

# factorial.bux's vres(g_k, fr_experts), with the experts in its first layer too.
g_k = fr_global(kv_conv_size=4)

# 2023 Mixtral, 2025 Qwen3 MoE, gpt-oss: the first layer's FFN routed, as every other's;
# a layer of experts' capacity at the same active parameters, every layer alike.
dense0 = embed
         fr_layer(hy_delta) fr_layer(hy_delta)^2 fr_layer(g_k(v=@v1))
         (fr_layer(hy_delta)^3 fr_layer(g_k(v=$v1)))^(layers // 4 - 1)
         fr_norm @h fr_out hy_mtp
model  = dense0

residual = hc(expansion=4)

# The hybrid's best at d512 (milestones.bux's scan), as the candidate's.
optimizer.lr = 2e-3
